.TH WRIT\-PUBKEY 1 2026-10-12 "writ 0.1.0" "writ manual"
.SH NAME
writ\-pubkey \- print the public key of a secret key
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nh
.ad l
\fBwrit pubkey\fR [\fB\-\-leaf\fR] [\fIKEYFILE\fR]
.ad
.hy
.SH DESCRIPTION
Print the public key of each secret key in KEYFILE, as a bundle item. Identity public keys are for \-\-next\-pub. A leaf public key can be the subject of a grant, for example to renew the leaf key.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
\fIKEYFILE\fR
a secret key file (default: standard input)
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-leaf\fR
the key is a leaf key
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
print help; \fB\-h\fR is short, \fB\-\-help\fR is long
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
0
success; for questions, the answer is yes
.TP
1
the answer is no: the check, verification, proof or name lookup was denied
.TP
2
an error: bad usage, unreadable input, or a failed operation
.SH EXAMPLES
Renew a leaf key for another day:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
writ pubkey \-\-leaf ci.key > ci.pub && writ grant \-i me ci.pub '(status)' \-\-expires 24h
.fi
.RE
